# Hermetic ship modules

Spaceship modules are pressure vessels. Visual/geometry joins must look and measure **airtight**.

## Mandatory

- **No slits / щелей:** daylight (sky, exterior) through any interior seam is a **hard fail**. Fix before authoring.
- Shared join profiles: opening, collar hole, canopy aft ring, and frames use the **same** opening size. Canopy/frame aft |Y|,|Z| must be **≥ hole − 1 cm**. Never a smaller glass plug inside a larger bevel.
- **Overlap, don’t butt:** seat glazing/frames ≥ 15 cm into the hull/collar along X. Prefer collar hole **slightly smaller** than glass so the opaque flange overlaps the pane edge.
- **Walkable interiors:** clear passage half-width ≥ 200 cm through cabin → nose; portal chamfer ≤ 20 cm.
- **Floor flush:** walkable floor top = `FLOOR_TOP_Z` (−184) into the nose; no step under the sill.
- **Glass seated on floor:** canopy sill Z ≈ `FLOOR_TOP_Z` (not floating). Floating panes show a white floor lip under glazing from outside.
- **Floor vs glazing:** floor outline under the canopy = **inner** face of glass/frame/cheek (fit after canopy exists). Past outer silhouette = lip; large inset = sky gap. Neither is acceptable.
- **No shell debris past canopy:** belly `floor_cut` / boolean cutters must not extend into the nose (end-caps look like floor shelves). `shell.maxX` stays near canopy join.
- **After mesh changes:** run hermetic bounds check; do not author while sky seams remain.

## Collision (related)

- Hollow shell/glass: **complex-as-simple**, never auto convex (fills cabin / blocks threshold).
- Floor: **simple box**. Open-forward shell if the nose is walkable.
- See skill `ship-module-creation` § Collision.

## Symptoms (blockers)

- Blue sky between white hull and glass/frame (side or corner slit)
- Canopy floating inside a larger hexagonal/beveled opening
- Triangular holes at wall–ceiling–window corners
- Floor ledge at glazing start **or** white slab past glass/hull from exterior
- Glass floating above the deck (underhang lip)
- Character blocked at canopy threshold despite a visible opening (convex/bulkhead)
- Character walks through cabin walls (shell collision missing / disabled)
